  ('Movies: directors and Best Picture winners', 'adult', 'mc', 'Only three films in Oscar history have swept all five major categories — Picture, Director, Actor, Actress, and Screenplay. Which of the following is one of them?', '{"options":["All About Eve","One Flew Over the Cuckoo''s Nest","Schindler''s List","Gone with the Wind"],"correctIndex":1}'::jsonb, false, 'ready', '{"verdict":"ready","notes":"Only three films have won all five major Oscars (Picture, Director, Actor, Actress, Screenplay): It Happened One Night (1934), One Flew Over the Cuckoo''s Nest (1975), and The Silence of the Lambs (1991). The distractors are all clearly wrong: All About Eve won neither Actor nor Actress in those categories that year; Schindler''s List did not win Actor or Actress; Gone with the Wind did not win Actor."}'::jsonb),
  ('Movies: directors and Best Picture winners', 'adult', 'mc', 'Which director helmed ''Annie Hall,'' ''Manhattan,'' and ''Crimes and Misdemeanors,'' yet famously never attended the Academy Awards ceremony despite multiple nominations?', '{"options":["Woody Allen","Stanley Kubrick","Roman Polanski","Terrence Malick"],"correctIndex":0}'::jsonb, false, 'ready', '{"verdict":"ready","notes":"Woody Allen directed all three films and is famously known for never attending the Oscars despite numerous nominations and wins; the other directors did not direct these films and don''t fit the clue."}'::jsonb),
