  ('World geography (challenging)', 'adult', 'mc', 'The Sahel is a semi-arid transition zone that runs across Africa between the Sahara Desert to the north and which biome to the south?', '{"options":["Tropical rainforest","Mediterranean shrubland","Sudanian savanna","Congo Basin wetlands"],"correctIndex":2}'::jsonb, false, 'ready', '{"verdict":"ready","notes":"The Sahel is indeed bordered to the south by the Sudanian savanna (also called the Sudan savanna), which is the well-established biome immediately south of the Sahel belt; the other options are geographically or ecologically incorrect as the southern boundary."}'::jsonb),
  ('World geography (challenging)', 'adult', 'mc', 'Which European microstate is entirely surrounded by Italy and sits on the slopes of Mount Titano, making it one of the world''s oldest republics?', '{"options":["Liechtenstein","Monaco","San Marino","Andorra"],"correctIndex":2}'::jsonb, false, 'ready', '{"verdict":"ready","notes":"San Marino is indeed entirely surrounded by Italy, built on Mount Titano, and is widely regarded as the world''s oldest republic (founded 301 AD); all distractors are clearly wrong — Liechtenstein borders Austria and Switzerland, Monaco borders France and the sea, and Andorra borders France and Spain."}'::jsonb),
  ('World geography (challenging)', 'adult', 'mc', 'The Strait of Malacca, one of the world''s most strategically vital shipping lanes, separates the Malay Peninsula from which large island?', '{"options":["Borneo","Java","Sulawesi","Sumatra"],"correctIndex":3}'::jsonb, false, 'ready', '{"verdict":"ready","notes":"The Strait of Malacca lies between the Malay Peninsula (to the northwest) and the island of Sumatra (to the southeast); Borneo, Java, and Sulawesi are clearly incorrect distractors."}'::jsonb),
