  ('Food and cooking around the world', 'all', 'mc', 'In Mexico, what are corn or flour flatbreads called that are used to wrap fillings like beans, meat, and cheese?', '{"options":["Crepes","Tortillas","Pitas","Naans"],"correctIndex":1}'::jsonb, false, 'ready', '{"verdict":"ready","notes":"Tortillas are indeed the traditional Mexican corn or flour flatbreads used to wrap fillings; crepes are French, pitas are Middle Eastern, and naans are South Asian, making all distractors clearly wrong."}'::jsonb),
